This is a known breaking change. Android deprecated `adjustResize`, so `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` no longer works in .NET 9+.

**.NET MAUI now ships `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll`** (enabled by default), which auto-scrolls focused inputs into view. However, it doesn't resize layouts — so a bottom-pinned input bar won't move up automatically.

### Fix: React to IME WindowInsets on Android

In your `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;

protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

    // Ensure edge-to-edge insets are delivered
    WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window!, false);

    var content = Window!.DecorView.FindViewById(Android.Resource.Id.Content)!;

    ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(content, new KeyboardInsetsListener());
}

private class KeyboardInsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        var navInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.NavigationBars());

        // Use whichever is taller — keyboard or nav bar
        int bottomPadding = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, navInsets.Bottom);
        v.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, bottomPadding);

        return insets;
    }
}
```

### Why this works

- `WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime()` gives you the **keyboard height** in real time.
- Setting bottom padding on the content view pushes your entire MAUI layout up.
- When the keyboard closes, `imeInsets.Bottom` returns to `0` and the nav bar inset takes over.

### Optional: Disable the auto-scroll manager

If `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` conflicts (double-scrolling), disable it globally:

```xml
<!-- Platforms/Android/AndroidManifest.xml -->
<application android:name="...">
  <meta-data
    android:name="Microsoft.Maui.KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Enabled"
    android:value="false" />
</application>
```

Or per-page in code:

```csharp
#if ANDROID
Microsoft.Maui.Platform.KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Disconnect();
#endif
```

This is the recommended pattern for chat-style UIs in .NET 10 on Android.
